      "closure_rationale": "Explicit contracts distinguish field-owned error offsets, accepted segment prefixes and final transactional output. Nonfinal complete fields remain AGAIN, offending bytes are not consumed, terminal failures retain absolute coordinates and structural refusal preserves control. Actual traces show why returning a local offset loses prior progress; propagation does not unwind resources. Both complete-buffer forms implement checked decimal accumulation and final admission: explicit goto/results and a strict C17 do-while statement macro. Side-effect counters require exactly one expression and destination evaluation, failure jumps, if/else composition and a caller-selected fresh identifier. The incremental first-principles parser retains sign/magnitude and numeric state only, with no parser library or borrowed-byte retention. Six compiler profiles execute4 anchors,9 compiled semantic controls and4 compiling learner-stub rejections. Independent grammar/whole-integer expectations match19548 complete cases, including every length0..6 string over the required alphabet, plus55959 signed/unsigned segmented cases at every selected split. Bounds,400-zero prefixes, embedded zero, canaries, absolute offsets and consumed prefixes are checked. Actual baseline ER_MUTANT3/4 are rejected separately. The changed representation supports a signed first field, nonnegative final total, repeated terminal observations, finite position refusal and scratch-buffer overwrite across three segments. GCC and Clang actually reject initializer use and deliberate temporary-name capture, accept a fresh-name if/else control and expose actual preprocessed tokens. No macro hygiene, caller return from inline function, automatic cleanup or universal-input proof is inferred. All13cost dimensions and seven equal-contract retained/explicit/macro timing samples are retained. Bounded author support only."
    },
